{"name":"Burnside","hex":"#d0a664","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Burnside","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Any of various places in Scotland, or elsewhere in the Anglo-Saxon world, named after the Scottish ones.","A topographic surname from Middle English for someone living near a burn (stream), or in any of the Scottish towns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Burnside"}],"entries":[{"title":"City of Burnside","blocks":[{"text":"The City of Burnside is a local government area in the South Australian city of Adelaide stretching from the Adelaide Parklands into the Adelaide foothills with an area of 2,753 hectares. It was founded in August 1856 as the District Council of Burnside, the name of a property of an early settler, and was classed as a city in 1943. The LGA is bounded by Adelaide, Adelaide Hills Council, Campbelltown, Mitcham, Norwood Payneham and St Peters and Unley."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Adelaide-LGA-Burnside-MJC.png/330px-Adelaide-LGA-Burnside-MJC.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City_of_Burnside"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Adelaide-LGA-Burnside-MJC.png/500px-Adelaide-LGA-Burnside-MJC.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Adelaide-LGA-Burnside-MJC.png/500px-Adelaide-LGA-Burnside-MJC.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdelaide-LGA-Burnside-MJC.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Skye_auldana_hills.jpg/500px-Skye_auldana_hills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Skye_auldana_hills.jpg/1280px-